; Index of the first item in the item table
;
; The item table (#R$A400 and #R$A500) holds one entry per index; entries
; before this index are zeros and are never used. This byte ($AD) is the
; index of the first real item, so the table has 256 - $AD = 83 items. It is
; read when a game starts (#R$87CA sets the present flag of every item from
; here to index $FF and copies this value to #R$85DE) and at every pass by
; #R$93D1 as the start of its loop. Nothing writes it while the game runs.
@label=FirstItemIndex
g$A3FF DEFB $AD
